From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Subject: [PATCH] t31: unpublish flat sensor symlinks on exit

remove_proc_subtree() can leave the flat /proc/jz/sensor symlinks
behind, and the next publish then trips the procfs "already
registered" warning. Remove them explicitly before dropping the root.

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
---
--- a/driver/common/tx_isp_sinfo.c
+++ b/driver/common/tx_isp_sinfo.c
@@ -1519,7 +1519,9 @@
 	}
 	mutex_unlock(&tx_isp_sinfo_lock);
 	if (root) {
-		/* remove_proc_subtree() below takes the flat symlinks too. */
+		/* Remove the flat symlinks explicitly: remove_proc_subtree()
+		 * can miss them when the proc root is detached separately. */
+		tx_isp_sinfo_flat_unpublish(root);
 		tx_isp_sinfo_flat_published = false;
 #if LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(5, 17, 0)
 		remove_proc_subtree("sensor", jz_root);
